DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>A December rate hike is now a near-certainty — plan for it.</b> Markets price a 100% chance of a Fed hike on 9 Dec and the 10Y is ~5.15%; avoid new floating-rate or high-interest debt and keep an emergency cash buffer.",
"<b>Don't let one stock's drama steer your money.</b> Nvidia fell ~13% this week and dragged AMD and Broadcom down Friday; a broad or equal-weight fund spreads that single-company risk.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Fear & Greed is 39 (Fear) and new lows swamped new highs (306 vs 26), so steady dollar-cost averaging beats guessing the bottom.",
"<b>Cash and short bonds still pay you to wait.</b> With the 2Y near 4.86% and a hike coming, short-term deposits or bond funds suit money you need within a year or two.",
"<b>Fuel relief is slow.</b> Brent fell 2.5% on the week on surplus talk, but diesel is still ~$6.06; don't budget for much cheaper fuel yet.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a rocket.</b> It just had its worst week since March (~$3,885); keep it a small slice and don't buy the dip with borrowed money.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC dropped to ~$68k, down ~10% on the week; only hold what you can leave alone.",
"<b>Thai investors: foreign money is coming back.</b> Foreigners bought ฿4.36B Friday as banks led the SET to 1,504.88; brokers see 1,490-1,520 ahead of Monday's Q3 GDP. In our dividend table, SPALI, ICHI, PTTEP, AP, TVO and PTT still trade at or below their buy zones (green) — check payout safety first.",
"<b>War headlines swing both ways.</b> Hormuz mines and drones vs. Europe joining Ukraine talks — don't bet big on a single peace or war headline."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 39 = Fear, little changed from 40 Thursday and well above 24 a week ago. Momentum and safe-haven demand read extreme fear; junk bonds read greed."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~46 = Elevated (steady): drones aimed at Bahrain were shot down and tankers hit mines in Hormuz, while Europe is set to join Ukraine talks."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 14.6 = extreme fear: the index is still below its recent trend after Friday's 0.4% dip."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 44.2 = fear, down from neutral; on the NYSE lows swamped highs Friday (26 highs vs 306 lows)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 52.2 = neutral, roughly unchanged."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 25.6 = fear: traders are still buying protection."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 50 = neutral on CNN's scale."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 21.2 = extreme fear, down from 29: stocks lagged even as bonds sold off."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 62.4 = greed: junk-bond demand is holding up despite higher rates."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 62 (from 61): the US downed Iranian drones heading for Bahrain and Mossad is urging renewed strikes. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 39 (unchanged): Europe is set to join the next talks, but Ukraine launched ~1,200 drones at Russia and Putin's hard line stands."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 80 (from 78): Iran said three tankers hit mines in Hormuz and drones were downed en route to Bahrain."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 15 (unchanged): the US-Iran channel is shut, but the Ukraine track is widening to Europe."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 33 (unchanged): no explicit nuclear threats, but Iran keeps its enriched uranium."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,562 Friday (−0.4%) as chips fell, but +2.5% on the week."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. +0.1% Friday to about 52,348."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −0.91% Friday to about 25,136 on the chip selloff; Nvidia reports 17 Nov."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~5.15% Friday (+4bp), touching 5.174% intraday."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$88.6 (−0.2%) Friday, −2.5% on the week as the IEA flagged a surplus."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$95.8, flat Friday after peaking at $97.13; −2.5% on the week."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.06/gal (AAA), down from $6.23 a week ago but still above $6; the 22 Sep record was $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,885, steady Friday but −4.7% on the week, its worst since March; support ~$3,850."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$68.2k = bearish: −4.4% in 24h and ~−10% on the week; $68k is the line to watch."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00% after September's hike, held on 28 Oct; next decision 8-9 Dec, where a hike is fully priced."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. October rose 0.4% MoM (est. 0.3%) and core 0.3% (est. 0.2%), a third straight upside surprise; no official YoY because of last year's data gap, well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. October rose 0.3% MoM (est. 0.4%) and 6.5% YoY, the highest since November 2022; core +0.3%."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). 100% for a December hike: ~89% for a quarter point and ~11% for a half point."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. ~103.2-103.4, the highest since April 2025, after its best week in two months."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. Hovering near 160 — the level where Japan has warned about intervention."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) in October; its raised outlook sent the stock up 24.7% on 11 Nov."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct (unanimous). Minutes say policy should stay accommodative, but low rates amid global tightening add financial-stability risk; next decision 23 Dec."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,504.88 Fri 13 Nov (+0.39%), led by banks; brokers see support ~1,490 and resistance ~1,520."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿4,355.85M on 13 Nov, a second straight day of buying after +฿1,711M on 12 Nov; local funds +฿382M."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};

