DASH.glossary.hl={m:"Breadth",d:"New highs = NYSE stocks at a 52-week high; new lows = at a 52-week low. Index up while lows still dominate = a narrow bounce. Latest session (Fri 13 Nov): 26 highs vs 306 lows (WSJ), the most lows in at least a month of our chart and worse than 39 vs 222 Thursday, even though the S&P fell only 0.4% and rose 2.5% on the week — rising yields and the chip selloff hit most stocks while a few big names held the index up. Lows have beaten highs on every session in our chart this month except 4 Nov; more highs than lows again would be the first sign of healing."};

